# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.
# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# GEMINI_MODEL: Centralized model identifier for Gemini processing.
# Verified Gemini model identifier: gemini-3.8-flash
GEMINI_MODEL="gemini-3.8-flash"

# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# VITE_BARCODE_API_URL: Optional custom endpoint for external barcode lookups (e.g. https://world.openfoodfacts.org/api/v2/product/{barcode}.json)
VITE_BARCODE_API_URL=""

# ==============================================================================
# SUPABASE CONFIGURATION (Authentication, PostgreSQL Database & Storage)
# ==============================================================================
# 1. Local Vite Development:
# Set these in your .env or .env.local file:
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=""
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""

# (Optional backward compatibility alias):
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=""

# 2. Vercel Deployments:
# When using Vercel's Supabase Integration, Vercel automatically exposes:
#   - SUPABASE_URL
#   - SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (or SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)
# vite.config.ts automatically detects and maps these into VITE_SUPABASE_URL
# and VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY for the client build.
# CRITICAL: SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are NEVER bundled into client code.
